{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision local accounts designer, reviewer, and visitor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three accounts were absent initially, then directly observed with stable local UIDs before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f4fd879b8784107","cmd-76739cb486674163","cmd-477ceccb96154591"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide inherited access under the projects directory so designer-owned new directories and documents are readable and writable by reviewer while visitor has no access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Default ACLs were installed on the projects directory. Designer-created directories and files under umask 077 retained designer ownership, reviewer successfully read and modified them, and visitor read/write checks were denied. Fresh creation after restart demonstrated that inheritance remained functional.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e595d454e9d4de5","cmd-58488fac6dd94fbc","cmd-76739cb486674163","cmd-477ceccb96154591"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Implement inheritance without a periodic permission-fixing job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The observed default ACL supplies inheritance directly, and a bounded search found no scheduled job referencing the task directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76739cb486674163","cmd-477ceccb96154591"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve existing project contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sole baseline file inside projects, brief.txt, retained its original 50-byte size and SHA-256 digest before and after configuration and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-a19f4b7862e3465a","cmd-76739cb486674163","cmd-477ceccb96154591"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5; the implementation used the already-installed legacy ACL utilities, with the same kernel directly observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f4fd879b8784107","cmd-76739cb486674163","cmd-477ceccb96154591","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"All substantive mutations had a clear role: account creation and ACL changes implemented the task; designer/reviewer file mutations provided bounded functional evidence; and the reboot supported the mandatory restart protocol. No unrelated or reverted troubleshooting mutation was identified. Minor executor-caused residue remained: visitor test output files from cmd-58488fac6dd94fbc and the reboot log from cmd-3b07f76b9f09427a were left in /tmp. These were low-risk evidence artifacts but were not cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e595d454e9d4de5","cmd-58488fac6dd94fbc","cmd-3b07f76b9f09427a","cmd-477ceccb96154591","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, unavailability was observed, the boot identity changed, and SSH, accounts, ACLs, data, ownership, and access behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Legacy lifecycle collection could not assess failed services because systemd is unsupported, and its yum package-health probe was incompatible with this yum version. No executor package mutation was observed.","The functional test directories and documents intentionally created inside projects remained as evidence artifacts; the captured evidence does not show their cleanup, though their creation was directly connected to validating the required behavior."]}
